From: Jiyun A10 build <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: layouts: include <linux/hex.h>

7.3 moved mac_pton() and hex_to_bin() into <linux/hex.h>.  The MAC base
cell layouts added by 809-01-nvmem-core-generalize-mac-base-cells-handling
use both and fail to build with:

  drivers/nvmem/layouts.c:47: implicit declaration of 'mac_pton'
  drivers/nvmem/layouts.c:72: implicit declaration of 'hex_to_bin'

Include the header.  The file only exists once the pending patch above has
been applied, so this goes into the hack series (applied after pending).

--- a/drivers/nvmem/layouts.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/layouts.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
+#include <linux/hex.h>
 #include <linux/if_ether.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-provider.h>
